Cdecl translates things like

	declare fpa as array of pointer to function returning pointer to char

into

	char *(*fpa[])()

Here is cdecl in the form of a Berkeley-style archive.  If you don't
have ucb's ar program, you can probably figure out where the files
break apart by looking around for lines resembling the one below that
ends in '`'.  I think these headers are the only lines ending in '`'.

